[Music]  finding the right job can be challenging  enough but now experts are warning  people to be on the lookout for scammers  posing as potential employers the Better  Business Bureau says fraud involving  fake job offers now ranks as the third  riskiest type of scam Americans ever  reported losing more than 2.9 million  dollars so far this year  vladimir duthiers of our streaming  network cbsn is here to tell us all  about it flat good morning good morning  experts have a warning if the job seems  too good to be true it likely is  employment scams are increasing giving  false hope to people looking for work  preying on those who are often already  struggling to make ends meet we spoke to  one woman who thought her financial  burdens were over when she received what  she thought was a dream job offer only  to be driven deeper into debt it was a  very nice email you know I'm considering  you please respond back tell me a little  bit about yourself where do you want to  see yourself in 3 to 5 years  Kathleen Boylan jumped at the  opportunity after the mother of two had  been searching for work on popular job  sites for months the position offered 90  thousand dollars a year to be the  administrative assistant to a man named  Stephen at a canadian-based company  when you saw that job offer this was a  godsend yeah I already started figuring  out what I was going to do to repair the  house I was behind on tuition payments  for my daughter's school so I was  excited welcome aboard  the next email read you will receive a  mail from FedEx with instructions as  promised Boylan got a check for $3500 in  the mail and directions to deposit it  through mobile ATM or branch which she  did here at her local Wells Fargo over  the next few days  Stephen kept her busy looking up flights  for a potential business trip even  sending this passport photo and when a  company bill needed to be paid he told  Boylan to buy reloadable cash cards so  he could pay it off  she bought 5 $500 cards and sent him the  codes on the back that's when Boylan  says the man she thought was her boss  stopped responding and reality  slowly sunk in you've been swindled yeah  the check was fraudulent Boylan lost  over $3,500 in total funds her bank says  she still owes there was like hope for  like two weeks that I'm gonna get back  on my feet again I'm gonna make things  right my kids gonna be able to not have  to worry about tuition and just to be  financially solvent you know it was just  that hurt job scams like these are on  the rise the Better Business Bureau  found it's the third riskiest scam for  consumers overall with an average of  more than six thousand dollars lost for  each victim  Catherine Hutt is BiBi B's national  spokesperson for all scams they either  want your money or they want your  identity and we've seen both with  employment scams Boylan now drives for a  limousine service and rideshare  companies to make ends meet but says the  money stolen hit her hard  I can't even look to the future it's  just like how do we get to next month in  this case the scammers used a real  company and the photo of an actual  employee so HUD says make sure you  verify by calling the company whilst  Fargo told us security is its top  priority but it doesn't comment on  specific ways it prevents fraud to  ensure its measures are effective the  bank also warns consumers to be aware  that scammers will often ask victims to  deposit bad checks and withdraw the  funds before the check is actually  cleared and your heart just goes out  yeah she's trying to make ends meet  she's got kids in school she can't pay  for their tuition and she's struggling  even in this economy and she says they  took away my future right so this is I  mean whoever did that Stevens we're in  America my guess I think of how many  more people out there like her - all  right glad thank you

